+# Changes from the released DyHGCN (chunyuanY/DyHGCN @ 54cd2c6)
+
+1. **torch_geometric ≥ 2 compatibility.** `GCNConv.weight` moved to `GCNConv.lin.weight`. Initialisation now uses `_gcn_w(conv)`. The model is unchanged.
+
+## G-repro (2026-10-14)
+- **What was run:** the released `run.py`, which hard-codes Memetracker and DyHGCN-H.
+- **Result:** Hits@100 0.582 (best epoch; the released loop selects on test) against the paper's 58.78% (Table 4), −1% relative. **Pass.**
+- Log: `../dyhgcn_repro_memetracker_H.log`.
+
+## Benchmark adapter (`dyhgcn_bench.py`)
+- **Variant:** DyHGCN-S, the paper's headline model, which uses the social graph.
+- **Selection:** on the validation split; the released loop selected on test.
+- **Truncation:** cascades are cut to their first 500 events. The released loader drops cascades longer than 500 entirely.
+
+## Data-pipeline bug fixes, used for the benchmark runs only (the model code is unchanged; the G-repro run used the released loader)
+
+**Training timestamps.** The released `DataConstruct.next()` reshuffles `_train_cascades` at the end of every epoch, but not `_train_cascades_timestamp`. From the second epoch on, timestamps no longer match their cascades. Both are now shuffled with the same seed.
+
+**Validation timestamps.** Released validation batches use the user-index lists as timestamps (`seq_timestamp = self._valid_cascades`). They now use `_valid_cascades_timestamp`.

